  "text_pages": [
    "Buddy Program\nESN UWB Pilsen\nAt the University of West Bohemia in Pilsen, there is a student organization \"ESN UWB Pilsen\" - group of volunteers (Czech students) who provide help to incoming exchange students and organize many cultural, sport and other type of activities during the academic year.\nHow it works?\nAround 1 month before the semester starts, Erasmus coordinator informs future Erasmus students about how to apply for a Buddy.\nWho is a buddy?\nA buddy is a Czech student who helps Erasmus incoming student. A buddy is not assigned automatically, each Erasmus student must apply for them. As soon as a buddy is assigned, he/she contacts the Erasmus student and starts the communication.\nWhat can a buddy do for you?\n- help you\nto find your way in a new environment (show you the city of Pilsen, nearest shopping mall and other facilites)\n- wait for your at the station upon your arrival in Pilsen to guide you to the accommodation (dormitory, flat...)\n- arrange necessary formalities (at the dormitory office, International Office, faculty etc.)\n- accompany you to a doctor / hospital\n- help with the communication at various places (dorm manager, bank, post office, exchange office, police station ...)\nContact and social media\nWebsite:\nhttps://www.esnuwbpilsen.cz/\nE-mail:\nboard@esnuwbpilsen.com\nSocial media:\nFacebook:\nwww.facebook.com/buddyuwb\nInstagram:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/esnuwbpilsen/\n© ZČU 1991–Thu Oct 08 10:02:20 UTC 2026\nCS\nEN\nCookies"
  ],
